                <head><seg type="margin">[472]</seg> *<hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Benavides, minister of foreign affairs, to Mr.
                            Perry, United States chargé
                        d’affaires.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of
                            State</hi>,<lb/><placeName><placeName type="venue"><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Palace</hi></placeName>, <placeName
                                type="city"><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Madrid</hi></placeName></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1865-03-21"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 21,
                        1865</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Reserving the privilege to communicate to
                    you whatever the authorities of the Ferrol may reply hereafter with respect to
                    the fraudulent increase of the crew of the corsair Stonewall, to which your
                    notes of the 7th instant refer, I have the honor now to communicate that the
                    captain-general of that marine department said, in a telegram the day before
                    yesterday to the minister of marine, that the Stonewall had not enlisted any men
                    at all.</p>
                <p>I avail myself of this occasion to renew, &amp;c., &amp;c.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A. BENAVIDES.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chargé d’affaires</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">of the United States.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
